# A Michaelis-Menten rule that deletes a whole homodimer. BioNetGen counts the
# substrate once per complex; NFsim's reactant list holds one match per
# subunit, so the law is handed twice the substrate there is. The law is not
# linear in that count, so it cannot be corrected as the rule fires, and NFsim
# stops with an error when it picks a complex that holds two matches.
begin model
begin parameters
  kcat  1
  Km    1000
end parameters
begin molecule types
  S(d)
  E()
end molecule types
begin seed species
  S(d!1).S(d!1)  1000
  E()            10
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules S_m S()
end observables
begin reaction rules
  SS_mm: S(d!1).S(d!1) + E() -> E() MM(kcat,Km)
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
  writeXML()
end actions
